<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese 1996 car sales up 8.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese 1996 car sales up 8.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new car registrations:</p>
<p>December 1996 20,151 vs 16,741 (up 20.4 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/Dec 1996 217,913 vs 201,471 (up 8.2 pct)</p>
<p>Total for year by manufacturers market share (percentage in brackets), comparative figures refer to same period 1995:</p>
<p>    Fiat	   32,783 (15.04) vs 32,187 (15.98)</p>
<p>    Opel	   31,207 (14.32) vs 31,863 (15.82)</p>
<p>    Renault	27,550 (12.64) vs 25,782 (12.80)</p>
<p>    Ford	   21,212 (9.73)  vs 17,459 (8.67)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen   17,932 (8.23)  vs 15,176 (7.53)</p>
<p>    Peugeot	13,966 (6.41)  vs 14,408 (7.15)</p>
<p>    Citroen	13,374 (6.14)  vs 10,341 (5.13)</p>
<p>    Rover	   8,862 (4.07)  vs  6,440 (3.20)</p>
<p>    Honda	   7,209 (3.31)  vs  6,912 (3.43)</p>
<p>    Seat	    7,072 (3.25)  vs  9,031 (4.48)</p>
<p>	  --Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
